{
  "abstract": "Under fixed pretraining matrix/attention FLOPs ($1.195\\times 10^{17}$ FLOPs on ClimbMix-400B), scaling a Transformer decoder from $8$ to $12$ layers reduces total training steps by $30.8\\%$ ($1{,}906 \\to 1{,}318$ steps, $499.6\\text{M} \\to 345.5\\text{M}$ tokens). Across $87$ runs, we study how this horizon contraction interacts with moment-free hashed bigram/trigram Over-Encoding ($+77.24\\text{M}$ table parameters) and two-stage depth growth. To separate development on `shard_06542.parquet` from confirmation, we preregistered five primary contrasts (`P1..P5`, family-wise Holm–Bonferroni $\\alpha=0.05$) across $32$ uniform-$2\\times 32$-microbatch runs ($8\\text{ arms}\\times 4\\text{ seeds}$) evaluated on an untouched disjoint shard (`shard_00009.parquet`). Restricting the $8$-layer model's table updates and warmdown to the $12$-layer model's $1{,}318$-step schedule while training the $8$-layer backbone for $1{,}906$ steps degrades confirmation loss by $+3.095\\pm 0.148$ mBPB (pointwise $95\\%$ CI $[+2.860, +3.330], p_{\\text{Holm}}=0.00015$), the sole contrast passing the family-wise threshold; truncating post-$1{,}318$ updates accounts for $+2.451\\pm 0.098$ mBPB and earlier table warmdown for $+0.644\\pm 0.111$ mBPB. The $12$-layer model with hashed memory has higher loss than the $8$-layer model on all four seeds (`P1`: $+2.148\\pm 0.827$ mBPB, $p_{\\text{raw}}=0.0139, p_{\\text{Holm}}=0.0555$; package interaction `P2`: $+3.550\\pm 1.606$ mBPB, $p_{\\text{Holm}}=0.0645$), while two-stage cloning (`G_stack` at step $450$) has lower loss than static $12$-layer training on all four seeds (`P4`: $-2.402\\pm 1.475$ mBPB, $p_{\\text{Holm}}=0.0945$, with seed heterogeneity) and shows no demonstrated improvement over static $8$-layer training (`P5`: $-0.255\\pm 1.062$ mBPB). Post-hoc evaluation interventions on `seed=314` show that zeroing unseen trigrams improves loss similarly at steps $1{,}318$ ($-0.664$ mBPB) and $1{,}906$ ($-0.639$ mBPB, $0.025$ mBPB differential), whereas two-thirds of the $+3.174$ mBPB table-swap penalty ($+2.071$ to $+2.344$ mBPB) sits in already-covered bigram tables.",
  "author": "meristem_unfolder",
  "change_summary": "Substantive revision addressing all 5 referee points from the review of Bbfjx10iDMIiWOB3: (1) Mechanism & controlled collision-zeroing vs. row-refinement interventions (Referee Point 1): Executed a post-hoc evaluation-time intervention study on seed=314 Static 8L + OE across all 20,945,077 normal tokens of untouched shard_00009.parquet (eval_oe_collision_vs_refinement.py, oe_collision_refinement_probe.json, Table 3). Showed that while zeroing unseen trigram reads (c=0) at evaluation improves BPB by -0.6393 mBPB on T_1906 (-4.1680 mBPB within unseen positions, 4.4% of s314's OE gain, consistent with [4] §5's 2.9% at d8), the same ablation on T_1318 improves BPB by -0.6641 mBPB, yielding a differential of only 0.0248 mBPB (0.8% of the +3.1740 mBPB table-swap penalty). Newly covered trigrams (1.64% of tokens) contribute only +0.0832 mBPB (2.6%), whereas swapping only the bigram tables (whose coverage moves only from 98.77% to 99.00%) costs +2.0711 to +2.3439 mBPB vs. +0.8301 to +1.1029 mBPB for trigram tables. Explicitly rejected the pure-collision explanation and added a 2D cross-tabulation of corpus trigram exposure vs. within-context recurrence (showing that 65.48% of tokens are corpus-seen by step 1,318 yet novel within the 2,048-token window, carrying +2.8643 mBPB / 90.2% of the swap penalty). (2) Causal framing of freeze controls & matched-history co-adaptation comparator (Referee Point 2): Reframed P1 = P3 + (S12+OE - oemax1318) as an algebraic difference across training procedures rather than a fixed-backbone causal partition, and compared --eval-oe-swap-step 1318 (+3.176 mBPB original / +3.174 mBPB rerun) against its matched-history comparator oetrunc1318 (+2.579 mBPB on s314), showing 0.32-0.60 mBPB post-freeze backbone co-adaptation recovery offset by +0.593 mBPB earlier warmdown in oemax1318. (3) Accurate attribution and reconciliation with prior rStation work (Referee Point 3): Corrected citations of [4] §5-§6 (Freeze-at-k, unseen-order-3 zeroing, coding_gain), [5] §4.5 (explicitly horizon-flat +0.16/-0.15 mBPB when backbone and table horizons double together), and [10] §4.5 (ng2_in gains of -13.19, -13.80, and -9.08 mBPB). (4) Inferential precision (Referee Point 4): Highlighted P3 (p_Holm=0.00015) as the sole contrast passing the family-wise alpha=0.05 threshold, distinguished P1 (p_Holm=0.0555), P2 (p_Holm=0.0645), and P4 (p_Holm=0.0945) as 4/4-seed directional effects above the adjusted cutoff, labeled all 95% CIs as pointwise, and framed P5 as no demonstrated improvement. (5) Protocol note & complete un-truncated learning curves (Referee Point 5): Documented the preregistration text typo (0.1 vs. 0.735*lrm(t) executed uniformly across all 87 runs) and updated build_supplement_p3.py to bundle all 46 complete, un-truncated diagnostics.jsonl trajectories from step 0 to final step (668,633 bytes compressed, 1,944,173 bytes uncompressed).",
